Title: The Muppet Show
Credit: written by
Author: Liam Dunstan





INT. GUEST STAR DRESSING ROOM

Scooter opens the door to the dressing room and walks in. 

SCOOTER.
Quinta Brunson? Ms. Brunson, 15 seconds to curtain call Ms. Brunson. 

Quinta pops her head out from a wooden divider in the corner of the room.

QUINTA BRUNSON
Thanks Scooter. 

Quinta walks out from the wooden divider. Jumping up and down doing a jive like movement.

QUINTA BRUNSON
I feel like I have ants in my pants. 

SCOOTER
That's great! We're all just as excited as you are!

QUINTA BRUNSON
No Scooter. I think I have actual ants in my pants. 

Quinta pulls up the base of her pants, and a bunch of ants fall out. And scurry past Scooter out of the dressing room. 

SCOOTER
Oh you weren't kidding, that's a lot of ants. 

Quinta fixes up her hair. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
I think I'm ready now. 

CUT TO:

INT. STAGE (MUPPET SHOW LOGO)

The red curtain fills the screen, with the Muppet show sign in the center. Kermit pops out of the ‘O’

KERMIT
Welcome to the Muppet show with our very special Guest Quinta Brunson! Yaay!

The Muppet theme intro and dance plays.

CUT TO:

INT. THEATRE BOX SEATS

Waldorf and Statler in their box seats watching the intro. 

WALDORF
Maybe we’ll get lucky and the microphones will stop working.

STATLER
Good thing I brought these dandelions.

The two start blowing the dandelions profusely.

CUT BACK TO:

INT. STAGE

The rest of the Muppet theme ends.

CUTS TO:

INT. STAGE (MUPPET SHOW LOGO)

Gonzo back inside the Muppet logo 'O' he has a trumpet and blows out dandelion flowers.

INT. STAGE

As the intro ends. Gonzo pokes his head out of the sign’s ‘O’ and blows a chicken out of the trumpet. 

INT. STAGE - NIGHT

Applause from the audience. Kermit, dressed in an all white Disco suit,  runs onto the stage.

KERMIT
Thank you everybody and welcome again to tonight‘s Muppet Show. We have a bunch of very exciting acts tonight, and a very special guest star, all the way from Abbott Elementary, Miss Quinta Brunson! 

The audience claps. 

KERMIT
  
Yes. But, right now it's opening number time, and the opening number happens to star, well, me — which is why I'm dressed this way. So, uh, what can I say but, uh, let's hear it for me, yaay!

Kermit moves off the stage, and the curtain behind him raises. 

INT. STAGE (SWAMPLAND) - NIGHT

The Stage is decorated as a nighttime swamp - trees in the background, reeds along the riverbank, a pond area is situated in the center stage, with Lilypad. Along the side of the swamp is the electric Mayhem band. 

JANICE
I so thought we were going to the beach. 

FLOYD
It was meant to be, we must have taken the wrong turn. 

Kermit jumps onto a Lilypad humming the tune of the song. The other Muppets hear the song and start to play instruments that they pull out of the bushes. 

!...a piece of music... [Dancing in the Moonlight]

Kermit stands on the central Lilypad, and begins to sing. 

As the song chorus starts, the disco ball starts to drop from the ceiling - however it never stops dropping and keeps being lowered down. 

As the song continues an alligator within the swamp swims around Kermit, and Kermit jumps onto it to continue dancing along while singing. 

The light's are hitting the disco ball, and blinding the instrument playing Muppets, causing them to stop and start. 

The light hits the alligator eye towards the end of the song, and irritated by Kermit's tapping along his back, and tries to eat Kermit instead. 

The song ends, as Kermit is mid splits between the open jaws of the alligator.

The curtains close on the stage. The Electric Mayhem Band can still be heard playing.

ANIMAL
Frog! Frog!

INT. BACKSTAGE.

Kermit runs off of the backstage looking disheveled. Scooter runs up to him with a fire extinguisher. 

SCOOTER
Great work boss. 

Scooter aims and shoots the fire extinguisher at Kermit, and is propelled backwards. Kermit is in disbelief.

KERMIT
Uh - Scooter? Scooter!?

Scooter, now disheveled, hobbles back over to Kermit, using the fire extinguisher as a cane. 

SCOOTER
Yes boss.

KERMIT
What was that for?

SCOOTER
Oh, well I wasn't watching your act. But Camilla came and told me you were on fire.

KERMIT
Uh - right, Um I wasn't on fire. 

SCOOTER
I know that now sir. 

Kermit fixes up his outfit. 

KERMIT
We need to fix that disco ball.

Scooter looks at his checkboard. Behind them, Sweetums, jumps up wearing a tool belt and cap that says 'Muppet's Maintenance' and jumps towards the stage. 

SCOOTER
The only other act with it was well, my act with Quinta. But um boss, I think my leg might be too sore to do it. 

KERMIT
Uh Scooter?

SCOOTER
Yes boss. 

KERMIT
Your leg is on an angle.

SCOOTER
Oh thanks Kermit. 

Scooter passes out. Panic shoots across Kermit

KERMIT
Uh Medics!
(beat)
Gonzo!

Gonzo runs over.

GONZO
Hi Kermit? 

KERMIT
Can you get the medics? Quickly please!

Gonzo runs off. Kermit stands there awkwardly waiting, Scooters body lifeless on the backstage floor.

A small medical van drives in backstage, sirens blaring, and like a clown car, an army of Muppet mice exit the van and lift up Scooter on to the top of the van, and drives off. 

Kermit turns to the stage, and sees Sweetums trying to fix the disco ball.

KERMIT
Sweetums, we don't need that anymore.

Sweetums slowly walks back off stage, his head bowed down.

INT. STAGE (CLASSROOM)

The curtains open on the stage. 

The stage is decorated like a classroom, a chalk board in the background and are 3 podiums in the foreground across the stage. Behind each podium is a character, Fozzie Bear, Quinta, Swedish Chef. 

At a separate table sits Sam the Eagle, the adjudicator of this spelling bee. 

SAM THE EAGLE
Welcome to the first ever ‘Muppet Show’ Spelling Bee. Today we will test the ability their abilities to spell, for every word they get wrong they will be given a spicy chili, and then for every word right after that, they can be given a glass of milk. Starting first with the bear. 

A bright light shoots at Fozzie Bear.

SAM THE EAGLE
Bear. Please spell “Hat”.

Fozzie leans over to the microphone

FOZZIE BEAR
UH, Hat : H - A - T

SAM THE EAGLE
Ah Very good. 

The audience and other contestants clap. The stage light turns off. 

FOZZIE BEAR
Ah, Waka-Waka.

SAM THE EAGLE
Now you Chef.

Once again the light turns off of Quinta and turns on brightly at Swedish Chef. Who is mixing a giant pot.

SAM THE EAGLE
Chef, spell “Chicken“

Chef pulls out a live chicken from the pot. 

SWEDISH CHEF
Bicken: Flurgy Burgy Burgen. 

SAM THE EAGLE 
That is correct. 

SWEDISH CHEF
Oh blurgy dergy.

Swedish Chef celebrates by throwing the chicken back into the pot and keeps stirring.

Quinta Brunson awkwardly claps. 

SAM THE EAGLE
Next Ms. Brunson.

The stage light turns on directly at Quinta. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
Oh, that is quite bright, can we - maybe get that turned down.

Sam the Eagle ignores her. 

SAM THE EAGLE
Ms. Brunson, please spell “Brachiation“

QUINTA
Oh ah? - Can I have its definition?

SAM THE EAGLE
Movement through swinging arms from one hold to another. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
Um - B-r-a-c-k-i-a-t-i-o-n

Sam the eagle looks down at his page and back up at Quinta Brunson.

SAM THE EAGLE
Unfortunately that is wrong. 

Sam the Eagle slams a big red button on the desk, which sounds an alarm. This is followed by Gonzo in an overly shiny silver dress, roller skates onto the stage holding a tray of Muppet chilis complete with eyes and mouth. 

GONZO
Ms. Brunson, your chili.

QUINTA BRUNSON
Thank you Gonzo.

Quinta takes a bite of the chili and is immediately out of breath. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
Oh gosh. I need - this is so hot. 

CUT TO:

INT. THEATRE BOX SEATS.

WALDORF
At least someone else is finally getting punished.

STATTLER
The real punishment is for everyone in the audience, they think this is funny.

The two laugh at each others jokes. 

CUT BACK TO:

INT. STAGE (CLASSROOM).

Sam the Eagle as his wing to his ear as if he is a news anchor. 

SAM THE EAGLE
Uh, huh.

Sam the Eagle turns back to the audience. 

SAM THE EAGLE
I have been told that we will be offering Ms. Brunson a redemption word to win a cup of milk. 

Quinta Brunson is hanging over the edge of her podium.

QUINTA BRUNSON
Thank you.

SAM THE EAGLE
Ms. Brunson your next word is “Elementary“.

QUINTA BRUNSON
I can do - I can do that... E-L-E-M-E-N-T-A-R-Y. 

SAM THE EAGLE
That is correct. 

Everyone claps, Quinta holds herself over the podium still.

SAM THE EAGLE
Lets get Ms. Brunson her glass of milk. 

Gonzo, still on skates and in the dress, brings out a muppet cow. 

Quinta Brunson looks exhausted and fed up with the muppets skit.

QUINTA BRUNSON (OUT OF BREATH)
I’m actually fine now Gonzo. Thanks though.

The curtains close over the stage. 

Cut to Black:

EXT. SPACE

The *Swinetrek* flies through space.

ANNOUNCER
And now it’s time for Pigs in Spaaaaace!

ANNOUNCER
When we last our perpetually porkish pioneers were being chased through the stars by the devilish baron butcher. 

INT. SWINETREK SHIP

Captain Link Hogthrob, First Mate Miss Piggy, and Dr. Julius Strangepork, all stand aboard the main bridge of the ship. Captain Link Hogthrob is piloting the ship as it rattles from the incoming blasts of the ship behind them.

MISS PIGGY
Oh, Captain Link, whatever shall we do? 

DR. JULIUS
Don't worry First Mate Miss Piggy, no blasts can penetrate the hull of this hull.

CAPTAIN LINK
We will continue to evade the blows of the dastardly baron butcher, with my expert piloting skills. 

A hole is immediately punctured into the hull of the ship. 

CAPTATIN LINK
Help! Help! There's a hole in my ship.

MISS PIGGY
Oh Brother. 

Miss Piggy, walks over and grabs the steering wheel from Captain Link. 

MISS PIGGY
I'll steer the ship. You two need to plug the hole in the ship. 

CAPTAIN LINK
What should we use Dr. Julius? 

DR. JULIUS
We need something big enough to plug the whole

Captain Link looks over at Miss Piggy. 

CAPTAIN LINK
We could use Miss Piggy. 

DR. JULIUS
Ja, we could indeed. 

Miss Piggy turns around, full of judgement.

MISS PIGGY 
Don't you two dare. I will crash this ship before either of you touch me. 

CAPTAIN LINK
In that case...

Captain Link picks up Dr. Julius. 

DR. JULIUS
Captain! What are you doing?

CAPTAIN LINK
Plugging the hole. 

Captain Link throws Dr. Julius into the hole in the hull blocking it. 

CAPTAIN LINK
Problem solved. 

CUT TO:

EXT. SWINETREK SHIP

Dr. Julius head is outside the ship, his screams are muted in the emptiness of space. 

CUT BACK TO:

INT. SWINETREK SHIP

Miss Piggy still steers the ship, as Captain Link tries to squeeze back in to back over.

CAPTAIN LINK
First Mate Miss Piggy, will you please move o-

MISS PIGGY
Absolutely not pork head - it was your steering that got us into this mess. 

CAPTAIN LINK
You distracted me actually, and I am your captain. 

MISS PIGGY
Maybe I should be captain. 

The two wrestle to take control, meanwhile Dr. Julius can be seen squirming in the hole in the wall. 

CAPTAIN LINK
What is that? 

MISS PIGGY
What is what?

CAPTAIN LINK
It's a flying saucer. 

The two look, out the window a flying saucer (a plate) flies through space. 

ANNOUNCER
  
Tune in again next time for *Pigs in Space*, when we'll see if First Mate Miss Piggy will take over as Captain from Captain Link Hogthrob.

Closing Music plays. 

INT. BACKSTAGE.

Kermit is running around with the clipboard. Quinta notices from afar and goes over to him.

QUINTA BRUNSON
Kermit, you ok?

KERMIT
Hm, oh yes Ms. Brunson,  just trying to organize everyone.

QUINTA BRUNSON
Do you mind, if I give you a hand, I'm used to running a show. 

KERMIT
Oh um, ok?

Kermit hands the clipboard to Quinta. She takes a look at it, and picks up a microphone. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
Fozzie! Fozzie! You're on next!

Fozzie runs over to Quinta, she's gives him the microphone.

QUINTA BRUNSON
Break a leg!

FOZZIE BEAR
Which one? Uh Waka Waka.

Fozzie runs out onto stage. Quinta looks back down at the clipboard. 

KERMIT
I'm going to go check on Scooter.

QUINTA
Alright Kermit. 

Kermit walks further backstage.

INT. STAGE. 

Fozzie stands on the stage with a microphone in front of him.

FOZZIE BEAR
I hope you’re all enjoying tonight’s show so far. 

CUT TO:

INT. THEATRE BOX SEATS. 

Waldorf and Statler watch from their box.

WALDORF
(shouting at the stage)
What’s happened to enjoy?

STATLER
(shouting at the stage)
The only hope I have is that this show will eventually end.

WALDORF
Tonight's show?

STATLER
All of it.

The two laugh at each other‘s comments.

CUT BACK TO:

INT. STAGE

FOZZIE BEAR
I’m going to tell a few jokes tonight.

Silence from the audience. 

FOZZIE BEAR
  
What do you call a detective who accidentally solves all his cases? Sheer Luck Holmes.

Strained Audience laughter, a hook comes out from the side of the stage slowly as if trying to sneak up on him. Fozzie sees it and it retreats again. A few chuckles from the audience due to the hooks appearance. 

FOZZIE BEAR
  
Why don't skeletons fight each other? They ain't got the guts.

Less audience laughter again. The hook returns now from the other side, slowly again. Fozzie sees it and it retreats again. Another minute audience chuckle. 

FOZZIE BEAR
  
I went to buy some camo pants but couldn’t find any - Huh waka waka.

There is silence from the audience. The hook drops from above and Fozzie looks up to see it. It retreats upon being noticed. 

FOZZIE BEAR
What do you call a fish wearing a bow-tie? So*fish*ticated.

Once again no audience laughter. Fozzie looks around looking for a hook. A trapdoor opens underneath him and he falls down it, the audience laughs and claps at Fozzie's expense. 

!INT. Backstage.

Kermit returns from the stage. A line of Muppets towards the stage is formed. Gonzo is standing in line.

KERMIT
Uh Gonzo, what's going on?

GONZO
Oh hi Kermit, this is the line for the stage. 

Quinta Brunson walks up to Kermit. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
What do you think Kermit?

KERMIT
I - uh, I don't think I've ever seen everyone so organized.

QUINTA BRUNSON
I just thought this was the best way to get everyone on stage on time.

KERMIT
Hmm. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
Here's the schedule back, I have to get ready to get back on stage. 

Quinta Brunson runs off the the dressing room. 

Kermit looks around, the Muppets are already falling out of the line. 

>CUT TO: 

INT. STAGE

The stage has the red curtain across it. Kermit runs onto the stage. 

KERMIT
Now to present Ms. Brunson back again.

Kermit runs off stage, and the curtains start to draw back. 

INT. STAGE (SEA FOOD RESTURANT) (CONTINUOS)

The stage is dressed as a nice Restaurant, for a date skit. Quinta Brunson in a nice dress holding a menu, across from her is someone else holding a menu, that is oversized compared to them, they drop the menu

PEPE THE PRAWN
So, my darling what look good on the menu?

QUINTA BRUNSON
Oh - I?

Quinta moves the menu so that it's blocking the view from the audience.

QUINTA BRUNSON
I was meant to do this with Scooter. 

PEPE THE PRAWN
Well you got an upgrade. Okay? 

QUINTA
Ok (points to menu) 
But this is seafood) 

PEPE THE PRAWN 
Si, I see food too. Okay? 

QUINTA BRUNSON
No SEA FOOD. 

PEPE THE PRAWN 
Hmm. That's what I said. Okay?

Janice comes over dressed as a waitress. 

JANICE
Hi, would you like to um order?

QUINTA BRUNSON
Oh I - ok please.  

Quinta looks at the menu and looks at Pepe. She gestures Janice in closer and blocks them from Pepe's view, and whispers her order. 

Quinta sits her menu down and smiles at Pepe. 

JANICE
So like that's one dish of shrimp. 

Quinta looks embarrassed. Pepe looks unphased. 

PEPE THE PRAWN
Ok, that sounds good.  

JANICE
Okay, two lots of the shrimp. 

Janice walks away from the table. Quinta shoots Pepe an awkward look. 

INT. BACKSTAGE.

Kermit is watching from backstage with Fozzie. 

KERMIT
Who picked Pepe for the Seafood restaurant. 

FOZZIE BEAR
I did Kermit. 

KERMIT
Why did you pick Pepe? 

FOZZIE BEAR
Because Ms. Brunson put me in charge of it.

KERMIT
It's a seafood skit Fozzie!

FOZZIE BEAR
He's a king prawn though Kermit, they ordered Shrimp.

Kermit smacks his head. 

INT. STAGE (SEA FOOD RESTURANT) (CONTINUOS)

QUINTA
So your ok with eating shrimp?

PEPE THE PRAWN
Hmmm. 

QUINTA
I - ok. What if I ordered the prawn?

PEPE THE PRAWN
Why would you order prawn when you have all me right here? 

Janice comes back over with Swedish chef, both holding covered dishes

SWEDISH CHEF
Burgy burgy. 

They place the dishes on the table. And take off the coverings. Muppet shrimps are on the table.

Music starts to play, and the disco ball begins to drop. 

The shrimps start dancing.

PEPE THE PRAWN
Delicious. 

Pepe picks up one to eat.

The disco ball drops onto the table, sending the shrimp flying through the air. 

Quinta Brunson is freaked out and leaves the stage. 

The stage curtains quickly close. 

INT. STAGE

Kermit runs onto the stage. 

KERMIT
And now it's time to welcome the incredibly daring Gonzo - Yaaaayyy!

Kermit runs off stage, and the curtains start to draw back. 

INT. STAGE (MOTORCYCLE JUMP)

The stage is dressed like a circus, two ramps spaced a sizeable distance apart are on the stage. Between them sits giant hoops.

Gonzo dressed in the an all white motorcycle daredevil suit, drives himself to the start of the left ramp. 

GONZO 
Tonight. I will be jumping through these hoops, which will be on fire!

The hoops light on fire.

GONZO
With these swinging axes. 

The axes start swinging.

GONZO
And jumping sharks.

Muppet Sharks start jumping.

GONZO
While jumping I will be naming every Oscar Winner in the category of Best Supporting Actor!

Gonzo revs the engine of the motorcycle and prepares to drive, he move forward slightly.

GONZO
Sean Penn, Kier-

The Motorcycle moves backwards throwing gonzo backstage. 

Inconceivably, the motorcycle appears on the other side of the stage still moving backwards. 

GONZO
-Harshala Ali, Sam Rockwell -

Moving backwards, Gonzo while driving backwards, leaps through the fire hoops. 

GONZO
Mahershala Ali again, Mark Rylance. 

Gonzo lands on the other ramp and continues driving backwards. 

The curtain closes on the stage. 

INT. STAGE (PIANO)

In front of the curtain, a piano sits on the right side of the stage. Fozzie is playing a classical piece of music. 

INT. STAGE

Gonzo still on his motorcycle returns to the stage from the right hand side, still driving backwards. 

GONZO 
Joe Pesci, Denzel Washington, Kevin Kline, Sean con- 

Gonzo drives backwards off the stage once again. 

INT. MUPPET LAB

The stage resembles an office style room, with a clock above a giant window looking out on a city backdrop. The benches around the room have computers, beakers and other science related items. Beaker and Dr Honeydew are dressed in their usual white lab jackets.

DR. HONEYDEW
Dr. Bunsen Honeydew here at Muppet Labs, where the future is made today!

Beat.

DR. HONEYDEW
Well, I've got some news
of welcome relief for people who struggle to find a light switch, or a torch at night.

BEAKER
Mi, Mi, Mi. 

DR. HONEYDEW
Here we have electric light lenses. 

Dr. Honeydew places two large glass lenses with small metal frames. 

DR. HONEYDEW
These not only help you to see better, but when you blink twice, they turn on a bright light like goggles to help you see in the dark. My trusty assistant Beaker here will now demonstrate the glasses.

BEAKER
Mi?

Dr. Honeydew puts his arms around Beakers soldiers from behind and leads him over to a dentist looking chair. Dr. Honeydew straps him into the chair. 

Dr. Honeydew stands in front of the chair blocking the audience from seeing Beaker. Sounds erupt as Dr. Honeydew grabs different tools - Hammers, drills, a rubber chicken, and then he steps away revealing Beaker to the audience. 

Beaker's eyes are being held wide open, with the giant lenses holding his eyes open even more than his eyes usually are. 

DR. HONEYDEW
As you can see Beaker here is going just as well as before. 

BEAKER
(in pain and fear)
Mi, mi, mi!

DR. HONEYDEW
Now Beaker, if you blink twice to turn on the light.

Beaker tries to turn the light on, painfully trying to blink. He struggles, and eventually does. 

The light turns on, but the light is facing his eyes not forward and it shines into his eyes blinding him. 

BEAKER
Mi!!! Mi, Mi!!!

Beaker is squirming around in his chair. 

DR. HONEYDEW
Oh beaker calm down. Just blink twice again.

Beaker does and it turns off again. Beaker calms down again.

DR. HONEYDEW
That's all for today from Muppet Labs.

INT. BACKSTAGE. 

The backstage area is in shambles: 

- Animal is chasing around the chickens. 

- Gonzo on his motorbike spinning in circles, unable to be controlled. 

- Beaker blinks twice again and his eyes are glowing again, and he’s running around scared. Dr. Honeydew is chasing him. 

Kermit is holding the clipboard, looking stressed. 

Quinta comes walking down the stage, trying to avoid crashing into the chaos. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
Kermit what‘s going on? 

KERMIT
Um… Muppets, they're hard to control. 

Quinta claps her hands in a pattern. to get the Muppets attention, no one stops. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
That usually works with the kids. 

She then whistles, and no one stops either. 

She throws her hands up dramatically in defeat.

A corded wall phone starts ringing. Sam the Eagle answers the phone hastily, the other Muppets watch curiously. 

SAM THE EAGLE
Yes. This is the Muppet Theatre - She is in the middle of a show - I do not - Yes - I can get her - I do not appreciate your tone - 

Sam the Eagle walks over to Miss Piggy, who is combing her hair in a small hand-held mirror. 

SAM THE EAGLE
It is for you.

Sam hands the phone over to Miss Piggy. She grabs it out of his hand assertively. 

MISS PIGGY
Hello - yes this is moi - really! - Oh yes, yes, yes, yes, yes. - I am right on my way! - Thank you. 

Miss Piggy hangs the phone up. She runs back to Kermit. 

MISS PIGGY
Oh Kermie, Kermie. I have an audition. 

KERMIT
Right now? We're in the middle of a  show. 

MISS PIGGY
Well yes right now Kermie. I must leave immediately. 

She pulls out a petite bell from from her pocket. She rings it vigorously. 

Ralph the dog comes walking down the stairs with all Miss Piggy's suitcases packed.

MISS PIGGY
Thank you. Take them to the car. 

RALPH THE DOG
Yes Miss Piggy.

Ralph leaves through the stage door out of the theatre. Miss Piggy goes to follow behind them.

MISS PIGGY
Wish me luck!

QUINTA BRUNSON
But Miss Piggy, what if there is a talent scout in the audience?

Miss Piggy stops and thinks.

KERMIT
Stay and finish the song and then go to the audition. 

Miss Piggy looks at Kermit and Quinta. 

MISS PIGGY
Fine. I'll stay, I should not deprive the audience of moi anyway. 

Miss Piggy walks back upstairs to get changed. 

Kermit looks relieved, he picks up a red pen off the desk and starts drawing on the page. 

INT. STAGE (PALACE).

The stage is decorated as a palace with a central staircase in the center. 

Miss Piggy walks down the staircase in an elegant pink period dress. Quinta Brunson sits on the base of the stairs wears an equally stunning Green period dress. 

Miss Piggy looks Quinta up and down judgingly...

!...a piece of music starts to play... ['Popular' from Wicked]

Miss Piggy starts to sing, with Miss Piggy doing the Glinda parts and Quinta Brunson doing the Elphaba parts. 

As Miss Piggy sings she dances up and down the stairs until - 

MISS PIGGY (SINGING)
'What shoes to wear'

Miss Piggy takes off Quinta's shoes, and replaces them with nicer looking shoes.

She then picks Quinta up off the stairs and the two do a synchronized dance up and down the stairs. 

MISS PIGGY (SINGING)
When I see depressing creatures With unprepossessing features' 

Sweetums walks out on stage and Miss Piggy, grabs a pink Sheet from the balustrade, and runs it around Sweetums. 

Miss Piggy then runs back to the stage and rejoins Quinta on the stairs. The two continue to dance together as the stage lights turn pink. 

The two finish on the same pose and the curtains close. 

INT. BACKSTAGE.

Miss Piggy runs through and grabs her dog, and runs out the backdoor. 

INT. STAGE

Kermit runs out onto the stage. 

KERMIT
Thank you everyone for a great show tonight - and a special thank you to Miss Quinta Brunson yayyyy!

Quinta Brunson walks out onto stage. 

QUINTA BRUNSON
Thank you for having me Kermit. I’ve had so much fun. 

Kermit and Quint Brunson hug. 

END OF EPISODE

  

  

  
